WP06 TypeScript contract proof

No TypeScript contracts were changed in WP06. The Rust protocol and core parser
mirror the WP05 TypeScript inventory evidence row contract.

Passed:
- cmd /c npm run test --workspace @ocentra-parent/activity-domain -- app-game.test.ts app-game-evidence-claim.test.ts app-game-identity.test.ts app-game-inventory.test.ts
  Result: 4 files passed, 22 tests passed.

Contract coverage reused from WP05:
- inventory rows must keep runtimeState and foregroundState at notClaimed;
- runningDurationMs and foregroundDurationMs must stay 0 for inventory rows;
- source kinds require matching identity/source refs;
- high-confidence display-only inventory is rejected;
- launcher installs stay separate from gameplay claims;
- stale and permission-limited states are preserved.
